			"Message": "style(Air): Enforce PascalCase naming in binary entry point\n\nCompletes the PascalCase normalization within the primary `Main` execution flow in `Source/Binary.rs`. This change aligns the local application state variable naming with the strict project-wide style guide recently applied to other modules.\n\nThe variable `app_state` has been renamed to `AppState` across all usages, including:\n- Initialization and timeout handling.\n- Dependency injection for `AuthenticationService`, `UpdateManager`, `DownloadManager`, and `FileIndexer`.\n- Instantiation of the `AirVinegRPCService`.\n- Background task closures (Connection Monitor and Health Monitor).\n- Shutdown sequence and final statistics collection.",
			"SHA": "3aca04f97d0aa056e4fc74995f4ccf1e70b1f7ba"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-02-01T11:51:47Z",
			"File": [
				"⡇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				54,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Air): Finalize PascalCase migration and correct external crate interactions\n\nThis commit addresses residual issues and compilation errors following the aggressive PascalCase refactoring across the `Air` element. It distinguishes between internal naming standards and external crate contracts, ensuring strict architectural hygiene.\n\nKey modifications include:\n- Reverting field access on the external `sysinfo` crate's `Memory` struct (`Total` -> `total`, `Free` -> `free`) to align with the library's snake_case convention, fixing compilation errors introduced by the internal refactoring.\n- Completing the PascalCase transition for internal `ApplicationState` configuration paths (`configuration` -> `Configuration`) in `Authentication` and `Downloader` modules.\n- Fixing a missed field access in the `ConfigurationManager` logging (`config.profile` -> `config.Profile`).\n- Refining the `Vine` gRPC server implementation (`AirVinegRPCService`) by removing duplicate imports, explicitly importing the `AirService` trait, and fully qualifying `Result` types as `std::result::Result` to resolve ambiguity with `tonic` status types.\n- Adding a missing error branch in `Authentication::WriteCredentials` to ensure the `Result` type contract is satisfied.",
			"SHA": "d51bfe241cf1933617dcfe1c3d722f4befffbbd0"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-02-01T11:33:49Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⣿⠁⠀⠀",
				54,
				23
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Air): Normalize naming conventions to PascalCase and consolidate gRPC service implementation\n\nThis commit enforces strict PascalCase naming conventions across the `Air` element, renaming struct fields, variables, and local identifiers (e.g., `cpu_limit_percent` -> `CPULimitPercent`, `utils` -> `Utility`). It also refactors the `Vine` gRPC server layer by consolidating the implementation into a single `AirVinegRPCService` module, removing the redundant `AirVinegRPCService_simple.rs` file.\n\nThe changes standardize the internal API consistency, aligning with the project's strict style guide and architectural hygiene. Updates include renaming the utility module from `utils` to `Utility` and adjusting all references in `ApplicationState`, `Configuration`, `Authentication`, `Downloader`, and `Metrics`. The generated gRPC bindings in `Source/Vine/Generated` have been updated to reflect PascalCase exports, and the module structure now re-exports the service traits cleanly.",
			"SHA": "fe6741c8ef3fa651858263a02582f3c483e0bb94"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-02-01T03:35:32Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⡇⠀⠀⠀",
				55,
				16
			],
			"Message": "style(Air): Enforce PascalCase naming convention across codebase\n\nThis commit enforces strict PascalCase formatting and naming normalization across the entire `Air` element, covering all modules including `Authentication`, `Configuration`, `Daemon`, `Downloader`, `HealthCheck`, `Resilience`, `Security`, `Tracing`, and `Vine`.\n\nKey modifications include:\n- Renaming all struct fields from `snake_case` to `PascalCase` (e.g., `app_state` -> `AppState`, `bind_address` -> `BindAddress`, `file_path` -> `FilePath`) to align with the project's strict style guide.\n- Updating method parameters, local variables, and public method signatures to follow PascalCase conventions (e.g., `validate_config` -> `ValidateConfig`).\n- Normalizing function calls, including extensions to standard library types (e.g., `duration_since` -> `DurationSince`).\n- Updating import paths and module references (e.g., `Air::` -> `AirLibrary::`) to match internal crate organization.\n\nThis completes the architectural standardization of the `Air` daemon's Rust implementation, ensuring consistency with the `Vine` protocol changes and minimizing visual noise in future diffs.",
			"SHA": "aec910b2eb921f558c8ad514c813ee5435992103"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-02-01T01:41:31Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				55,
				1
			],
			"Message": "style(Air/Vine): Enforce code formatting in simplified gRPC server\n\nThis commit applies strict code formatting and structural normalization to the `AirVinegRPCService_simple.rs` file, continuing the hygiene standards enforced across the Air codebase.\n\nKey adjustments include:\n- Updating import paths to reference the renamed `Vine::Generated::Air` module, aligning with the recent PascalCase module restructuring.\n- Removing redundant whitespace around type annotations (e.g., `Arc<ApplicationState>`, `request:Request`).\n- Normalizing struct literal formatting and match arm expressions.\n- Updating utility calls to match PascalCase conventions (e.g., `current_timestamp()` -> `CurrentTimestamp()`).\n\nThis ensures the simplified `Air` gRPC service implementation adheres to the project's consistent style guide, minimizing visual noise in future diffs.",
			"SHA": "34d9b2ef4c81c7932e8c92dffb55030e88ebcd77"
		}
